    "body": "Fixes #42025\n\n## Problem\n{Visual}Q stores an extra multicursor at the primary position. If a mapping edits the buffer, the primary moves before multicursor deduplication and the mapping is replayed there.\n\n## Fix\nDo not create a second cursor at the primary line during Visual Q. Add regression coverage for an editing mapping and update cursor-count assertions.\n\n## Tests\n- cmake --build build -j2\n- cmake -E env TEST_FILE=test/functional/editor/mcursor_spec.lua TEST_FILTER=42025 cmake --build build --target functionaltest (1 passed)\n- cmake -E env TEST_FILE=test/functional/editor/mcursor_spec.lua cmake --build build --target functionaltest (162 passed, 2 expected skips)\n- cmake --build build --target unittest -j2 (809 passed, 7 skipped, 12 failures in POSIX permission and case-semantics tests on the mounted Windows filesystem)\n- cmake --build build --target functionaltest -j2 (partial; stopped at a mounted-Windows socket limitation after earlier tests passed)\n- git diff --check\n\n## Limitations\nNative Windows CMake configure could not link because the host lacks MSVC/Windows SDK libraries (oldnames.lib and msvcrtd.lib). The build and focused tests ran in Ubuntu 22.04 WSL, with the checkout required under G:. StyLua and ts_query_ls were unavailable; their repository targets were attempted and recorded as unavailable. Windows-specific CI and Zig checks were not runnable on this host.\n\n## AI disclosure\nAI assistance was used to inspect, implement, test, and review this patch. I reviewed the final diff and test results.",
